WEBVTT

00:08.820 --> 00:09.980
Be careful.

00:09.980 --> 00:11.570
Thanks for the help.

00:11.570 --> 00:13.070
I appreciate it.

00:13.070 --> 00:13.490
No worry.

00:14.360 --> 00:18.280
Our only option is to rely on these kids.

00:18.280 --> 00:19.450
You're good to go!

00:20.250 --> 00:23.960
This same sliver is said to shine within people's hearts.

00:26.420 --> 00:30.260
So you're saying every member of Team Gargouille will participate?

00:30.260 --> 00:31.420
Yes.

00:31.420 --> 00:35.340
We all want to know what happened to Minashi
and his friends, so we want to head to Yomijima.

00:35.930 --> 00:37.760
We want to learn about the Abornines, too.

00:37.760 --> 00:40.390
Are there really Arbornines there?

00:40.390 --> 00:41.520
Yeah.

00:41.520 --> 00:45.060
Back when we lived on the island, they were all over.

00:45.560 --> 00:49.400
Maybe it can restore Emiru and the others...

00:49.400 --> 00:54.490
In any case, we'll operate covertly early in the morning.

00:55.320 --> 00:57.070
How are we getting to the island?

00:57.070 --> 00:59.700
Is it possible to borrow an SDF carrier?

01:00.410 --> 01:04.620
A few have volunteered to assist us,

01:04.620 --> 01:09.460
but unfortunately I am unable to borrow a carrier incognito.

01:09.460 --> 01:12.710
However, there is one place that'll have a plane we can use.

01:13.760 --> 01:15.090
Where's that?

01:15.090 --> 01:17.050
Inside the Lightless Realm.

01:19.100 --> 01:22.810
We're going to head towards
the abandoned Atsugi Base first.

01:28.730 --> 01:32.110
That light was someone's hope.

01:32.110 --> 01:39.700
Approaching their time of departure, they were left with only that to believe in.

01:39.700 --> 01:42.740
We're finally going into the Lightless Realm, huh?

01:42.740 --> 01:47.500
But won't you be affected the most, Suzaki-san? Since you're not a Linker and all.

01:47.500 --> 01:49.460
Most likely.

01:49.460 --> 01:51.630
I'm counting on all of you.

01:55.630 --> 01:57.760
All right. Let's head out!

02:12.690 --> 02:21.030
The ink on today's graffiti runs

02:21.030 --> 02:32.040
A bicycle that has been abandoned awaits someone's return

02:32.040 --> 02:43.010
When we realized, it was up for us to choose if our existence is a replica or not

02:43.010 --> 02:47.390
Where is our proof?

02:47.390 --> 02:52.480
It's mankinds nature to come together

02:52.480 --> 02:57.530
Our love and bonds are things we can trust

02:57.530 --> 03:02.320
My sins are to be doubted

03:02.320 --> 03:08.660
The light I saw when you first held out your right hand

03:12.040 --> 03:17.510
We really are

03:26.010 --> 03:28.220
The Dark Metal

03:32.480 --> 03:36.940
Episode 18
The Truth of Yomijima

03:38.150 --> 03:41.110
Looks like they've finally entered the Lightless Realm.

03:41.110 --> 03:42.820
Be careful, Susan...

03:42.820 --> 03:43.740
The rest of you, too.

03:44.370 --> 03:46.410
Good morning.

03:46.410 --> 03:49.410
Good morning. You're early today.

03:49.410 --> 03:54.630
I ended up staying up all night checking the data on the three MA-Vesses.

03:57.550 --> 04:03.720
There were no signs of Necrometal during the checkup on any of the three, including Akashi.

04:05.390 --> 04:07.050
I see.

04:07.050 --> 04:08.890
Is that all you have to say?

04:08.890 --> 04:13.770
Akashi was in the Lightless Realm for several days, yet...

04:15.350 --> 04:18.480
That kind of information is something I don't need.

04:18.480 --> 04:21.860
But if we can figure out the reason why—

04:21.860 --> 04:24.360
I said I don't need it!

04:24.360 --> 04:29.240
Without the MA-Vess, there is no
chance of entering the Lightless Realm.

04:29.240 --> 04:32.830
It's completely unnecessary from
whatever angle you look at it from.

04:33.370 --> 04:34.790
He's so...

04:35.250 --> 04:39.550
By the way, there's some data that just doesn't add up.

04:39.960 --> 04:41.130
Can I have a minute?

04:41.130 --> 04:42.800
Uh, sure...

04:43.880 --> 04:52.350
Saginuma Akashi's resonance rate should be at its peak based on transitions from other data.

04:52.350 --> 04:56.850
So why do you think it reached only 87% of its maximum?

04:56.850 --> 04:57.860
I don't know.

04:57.860 --> 04:58.860
That's strange.

04:58.860 --> 05:02.780
I really hope you didn't alter the data.

05:06.780 --> 05:10.160
His resonance rate is higher than the theoretical limit?

05:10.160 --> 05:11.160
Hey...

05:11.870 --> 05:17.790
What was the meaning of hiding such important data from me?!

05:17.790 --> 05:19.380
I'm terribly sorry.

05:19.840 --> 05:24.720
I at least trusted you as a fellow researcher, but you betray me instead!

05:25.470 --> 05:28.260
That's it, you roach woman!

05:28.260 --> 05:30.390
Call Akashi here right now!

05:30.390 --> 05:32.640
I'll investigate myself!

05:32.640 --> 05:34.270
Akashi isn't here.

05:34.270 --> 05:34.980
What?

05:34.980 --> 05:37.690
He's headed towards Yomijima.

05:38.190 --> 05:39.400
I see...

05:39.400 --> 05:43.030
So your data alteration was to buy him time to go there.

05:45.740 --> 05:49.870
Maki Minashi must've regained his memory.

05:49.870 --> 05:52.200
That's worth a celebration.

05:55.750 --> 05:58.000
This is Atsugi Base?

05:59.500 --> 05:59.580
U.S. NAVY               ATSUGI AIR BASE

06:06.170 --> 06:07.880
Dammit! My vision's starting to go blurry.

06:12.470 --> 06:13.930
Suzaki-san, are you okay?

06:13.930 --> 06:15.640
Then get outta here fast!

06:15.640 --> 06:16.980
I can't!

06:16.980 --> 06:17.890
<i>He's</i> there!

06:17.890 --> 06:19.440
No one's there!

06:19.440 --> 06:21.440
The Lightless Realm's playing tricks on you!

06:21.440 --> 06:22.730
Don't give in to it!

06:22.730 --> 06:24.610
Hold your mind steady!

06:28.450 --> 06:29.990
You're right...

06:29.990 --> 06:32.990
Because he's no longer around!

06:38.210 --> 06:40.960
The carrier we can possibly use is over there!

06:50.800 --> 06:52.430
Iwato, go on ahead!

06:52.430 --> 06:53.100
Got it!

06:54.390 --> 06:55.850
Do you know how to fly it?

06:55.850 --> 06:59.020
I read the manual all last night!

06:59.020 --> 06:59.730
It's your first time?

06:59.730 --> 07:03.400
Manuals are written so that even novices can!

07:03.400 --> 07:04.480
Sit over there!

07:04.480 --> 07:05.400
R-Right.

07:09.150 --> 07:11.700
Hurry, Raika, Akashi!

07:24.210 --> 07:27.170
Ow! Take it easy!

07:27.170 --> 07:29.170
Jeez, stop moving!

07:29.170 --> 07:31.590
Machine guns kick back more than I thought.

07:31.590 --> 07:32.470
Idiot.

07:32.930 --> 07:34.800
Don't overdo it.

07:37.140 --> 07:38.180
What?

07:38.180 --> 07:39.350
Nothing...

07:40.350 --> 07:44.190
In the short time you were away, the air around you has changed.

07:49.110 --> 07:50.530
Maybe.

07:50.530 --> 07:51.820
There you go.

07:51.820 --> 07:53.200
Thank you.

07:53.200 --> 07:55.620
The two of you are a bit different as well.

07:58.040 --> 07:59.750
I could say the same for you too.

08:06.250 --> 08:11.340
There was someone I was going to marry, but an accident five years ago prevented that from happening.

08:12.720 --> 08:16.850
I thought I was all right by now, but I'm really not.

08:17.600 --> 08:22.480
Even if you try to force yourself to forget,
those thoughts continue to linger like a bad aftertaste.

08:23.640 --> 08:24.600
Minashi...

08:34.740 --> 08:35.410
I see it!

08:36.320 --> 08:38.370
That's Yomijima?

08:40.830 --> 08:42.790
Sasame's birthplace...

08:49.130 --> 08:54.130
When we were here, the deity's power from
within the Lightless Stone kept the island hidden.

08:54.130 --> 08:56.760
That's why it wasn't on any of the maps.

08:56.760 --> 08:58.720
Lightless Stone?

08:58.720 --> 09:00.770
It was the island's guardian.

09:00.770 --> 09:04.810
The Lightless Realm's source that's inside the Corpse now...

09:04.810 --> 09:06.730
The root of all evil, huh?

09:06.730 --> 09:08.360
And the Arbornine?

09:09.020 --> 09:12.740
Strangely enough, I don't smell any Arbornine.

09:18.160 --> 09:19.620
The Arbornine...

09:19.620 --> 09:22.240
These are Arbornine?

09:22.240 --> 09:24.500
They're all withered.

09:24.500 --> 09:27.080
Beautiful flowers bloom on them in the spring.

09:30.090 --> 09:33.510
We all used to see the flowers in the garden together.

09:38.840 --> 09:40.180
That's right...

09:40.180 --> 09:43.560
This was the entrance, and the living room was here.

09:43.560 --> 09:45.140
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

09:45.890 --> 09:48.520
We slept in the next room...

09:48.520 --> 09:53.650
And Sasame and Tsugumi lived in the house across the garden.

09:54.070 --> 09:57.990
The three of us played together every day

09:57.990 --> 10:00.910
because there were no other children on the island.

10:14.590 --> 10:15.800
This is...

10:15.800 --> 10:17.970
An old emblem IX used.

10:18.760 --> 10:23.930
Everyone was brought to this building, and none of them ever came home.

10:49.500 --> 10:51.040
Hey, are you all right?

10:55.920 --> 10:58.510
Stop it! Stay away! Stay away!

11:08.770 --> 11:10.770
This isn't the right fit either...

11:10.770 --> 11:14.690
Guess I'll administer a bit more stimulant.

11:14.690 --> 11:15.860
Natsuiri...

11:20.360 --> 11:22.410
Oh, that was so close!

11:22.410 --> 11:24.200
It was going pretty well, too.

11:24.990 --> 11:27.790
But all in all, it's going well.

11:33.210 --> 11:37.670
They couldn't take the pain and chose to end their own lives...

11:37.670 --> 11:40.130
Why can't they see it from my point of view?

11:41.760 --> 11:44.140
Such horrible things happened here?

11:53.600 --> 11:55.610
What's going on?

11:55.610 --> 11:59.070
I think they had visions of what happened here in the past...

12:02.910 --> 12:03.740
What's that?

12:20.340 --> 12:23.800
What a coincidence that I'd run into you here.

12:24.800 --> 12:26.010
It's unmanned?

12:26.010 --> 12:32.310
I painstakingly preserved it on this island. It is the very first MA-Vess.

12:32.310 --> 12:36.860
It uses a resonance module that copied a human persona.

12:36.860 --> 12:38.980
You could call it the ancestor of the LIM.

12:40.650 --> 12:41.940
Minashi?

12:43.900 --> 12:50.370
For you, there should be a more
proper term to call it, Minashi-kun.

12:56.750 --> 12:58.000
Big Sister...

13:00.670 --> 13:01.590
Seriously?

13:02.300 --> 13:03.550
Big Sister...

13:05.760 --> 13:11.430
Understanding can be reached without
words through each other's consciousness.

13:11.430 --> 13:14.560
I've named such people "Linkers."

13:14.560 --> 13:16.730
What a load of crap.

13:16.730 --> 13:21.440
If my theories are correct, anyone can become a Linker!

13:21.440 --> 13:23.190
What a waste of time.

13:23.190 --> 13:31.240
One application is this resonance module.
A Linker can control this machine with mere thoughts!

13:31.240 --> 13:33.620
This is truly revolutionary technology...

13:38.080 --> 13:39.250
Those dimwits!

13:42.210 --> 13:45.760
Bunch of incompetents that can't even grasp this theory.

13:45.760 --> 13:50.930
They can just keep preserving their
worthless pride by looking down on me.

13:51.720 --> 13:55.480
They're all truly good-for-nothings...

13:55.480 --> 13:58.190
Should I just die already?

13:58.190 --> 14:00.520
I don't think that's a good idea.

14:06.780 --> 14:14.040
If your research advances, is it true anyone can
come to a correct understanding without speaking?

14:14.040 --> 14:16.080
What's with this girl?

14:16.080 --> 14:17.830
I'm Maki Mimei.

14:17.830 --> 14:18.620
A Linker?

14:19.920 --> 14:22.090
What you just said...

14:22.090 --> 14:24.920
What do you think isn't a good idea?

14:24.920 --> 14:27.260
That you were going to choose death.

14:30.680 --> 14:33.600
To answer your question...

14:33.600 --> 14:38.810
I'm sure I can as long as you, a Linker, cooperates.

14:38.810 --> 14:40.650
That's wonderful!

15:04.130 --> 15:05.000
Looking good!

15:09.800 --> 15:10.800
Well?

15:10.800 --> 15:14.720
They finally decided to fund this research project.

15:15.220 --> 15:16.390
I'm so glad.

15:16.390 --> 15:20.690
But their objective is merely an interface driven by thoughts.

15:22.900 --> 15:27.860
They're still as skeptical as ever
about linking people's thoughts.

15:28.320 --> 15:29.490
It's all right.

15:29.490 --> 15:31.530
You can do it.

15:31.530 --> 15:33.820
Because your research is wonderful.

15:34.620 --> 15:36.290
I'm sure they'll recognize it.

15:41.830 --> 15:46.710
With your research, people will
someday be connected without words.

15:48.710 --> 15:51.590
I want Linkers besides you.

15:52.220 --> 15:56.220
To progress with my research, I need more samples.

16:02.100 --> 16:05.060
Yomijima... Is that the place?

16:05.060 --> 16:08.070
Yes... The island where I was born.

16:11.070 --> 16:14.570
As you can see, it's a place left behind by the times.

16:25.250 --> 16:28.170
So they're really all Linkers?

16:28.170 --> 16:29.130
Yes.

16:29.550 --> 16:33.840
But those children may be the last generation born on this island.

16:34.300 --> 16:40.560
Before that happens, I want you to create a world where we don't have to continue living in hiding.

16:41.600 --> 16:43.520
I believe you can do it.

16:44.060 --> 16:45.770
Of course.

16:45.770 --> 16:47.480
I'll fulfill that promise.

16:52.400 --> 16:54.910
Stop this cruelty!

16:54.910 --> 16:57.320
This is a necessary experiment.

16:57.320 --> 16:58.280
Are you okay?

16:58.280 --> 17:00.120
I'll help you out right—

17:00.120 --> 17:00.990
Hands off!

17:02.750 --> 17:06.210
The pain they feel is proof that they're resonating!

17:06.880 --> 17:10.170
Thanks to you, my research has taken a giant leap forward!

17:10.710 --> 17:13.300
Come on, praise me! Well, come on!

17:15.720 --> 17:16.470
Cancel it!

17:16.470 --> 17:20.600
The resonance research has almost borne fruit!

17:20.600 --> 17:22.770
And what did you do to accomplish that?

17:22.770 --> 17:25.230
What did I do? Experiments, of course...

17:25.730 --> 17:27.810
The way you go about it is the issue!

17:27.810 --> 17:32.730
The project committee didn't
approve such inhumane experiments!

17:32.730 --> 17:37.530
If the truth of this got out, it would deal
massive damage to politicians and financiers!

17:37.530 --> 17:39.830
Every last experiment was necessary!

17:39.830 --> 17:41.990
All the deaths were caused by suicide...

17:41.990 --> 17:43.750
It's already been decided.

17:43.750 --> 17:46.250
This experiment facility will be disposed of.

17:48.210 --> 17:50.170
I'll have someone pick you up later.

17:50.170 --> 17:52.380
Make sure you're prepared to leave!

17:54.260 --> 17:55.920
Those dimwits...

17:55.920 --> 18:00.140
Let's leave them all aside and continue the experiments ourselves, Mimei.

18:01.510 --> 18:04.430
I shouldn't have brought you to this island...

18:06.310 --> 18:07.890
I'm sorry.

18:07.890 --> 18:11.570
My desire turned you into what you are now.

18:11.570 --> 18:13.650
What are you saying?

18:13.650 --> 18:15.940
I'm saying it's over.

18:15.940 --> 18:17.110
You're...

18:17.110 --> 18:18.660
You're kidding, right?

18:19.950 --> 18:21.620
How pathetic...

18:34.090 --> 18:39.050
Mimei... Mimei... Mimei... Mimei... Mimei!

19:00.160 --> 19:02.320
I don't think that's a good idea.

19:02.320 --> 19:06.620
With your research, people will
someday be connected without words.

19:11.630 --> 19:15.130
One application is this resonance...

19:15.130 --> 19:17.630
I believe you can do it.

19:18.260 --> 19:19.720
I'm sorry.

19:19.720 --> 19:22.640
I want to keep staying at his side forever.

19:34.940 --> 19:37.610
This is the resonance response?

19:37.610 --> 19:39.780
This is the worst feeling...

19:40.240 --> 19:44.280
You were the worst, and yet the best at the same time...

19:48.750 --> 19:52.040
You might be more aware of what happened after.

19:52.620 --> 19:58.000
You guys created the Lightless
Realm to exact revenge upon us, right?

20:00.470 --> 20:02.090
What's so funny?

20:02.090 --> 20:04.300
Nah, it's nothing.

20:04.300 --> 20:05.850
I'm just ever so grateful.

20:05.850 --> 20:13.150
When you guys created the Lightless Realm,
my research took an even greater step forward.

20:13.150 --> 20:17.610
Originally, my research was going to be cut short.

20:17.610 --> 20:23.160
But because a LIM was necessary to enter that place...

20:23.160 --> 20:24.820
If you...

20:24.820 --> 20:30.870
If you weren't around, Tsugumi wouldn't have made the Lightless Realm!

20:30.870 --> 20:32.410
That's right.

20:32.410 --> 20:36.590
And none of you would have met one another.

20:36.590 --> 20:41.210
And you would have led ordinary lives for as long as possible

20:41.210 --> 20:46.390
with all the lukewarm anger, sorrow, and joy.

20:46.390 --> 20:47.930
Isn't this great?

20:48.510 --> 20:55.770
Akashi-kun, you would've been able to blame your cowardice on your brother and keep hating him.

20:56.190 --> 20:58.570
When we get back, I'll make you spill it all!

20:58.570 --> 21:01.440
Your sins and everything else!

21:01.440 --> 21:04.400
Sins? That's rude.

21:04.400 --> 21:07.120
Call them achievements and praise me instead!

21:07.120 --> 21:08.370
You're one messed up motherfucker!

21:08.370 --> 21:11.160
But it's unfortunate...

21:11.160 --> 21:13.540
You guys can't go back.

21:13.540 --> 21:15.870
I'll have you all turned into Necrometal right here.

21:16.370 --> 21:22.920
I may have enough LIMs, but I still have a dream that I want to make reality.

21:22.920 --> 21:27.180
If you became Necrometal, you'd be good samples.

21:27.180 --> 21:28.600
Damn you...

21:28.600 --> 21:29.850
Just how far are you willing to go?

21:31.220 --> 21:32.890
I can't forgive...

21:32.890 --> 21:35.350
We can never forgive...

21:41.150 --> 21:43.280
Can't forgive...

21:43.280 --> 21:48.780
Give them Admonitions and turn them all into corpses...

21:48.780 --> 21:50.780
What is it this time?

21:50.780 --> 21:52.620
Where are these voices coming from?

21:53.500 --> 21:58.830
Can't forgive...

22:08.640 --> 22:11.050
The Lightless Realm?

22:15.600 --> 22:19.310
Can't forgive... Can't forgive...

22:27.900 --> 22:31.990
Heh, you die on your own but come back as ghosts?

22:31.990 --> 22:34.910
You really are idiots.

22:56.390 --> 23:00.440
You lose your mind, you crash; a nervous breakdown

23:05.190 --> 23:10.070
You try to change your life, you jump another let down

23:10.070 --> 23:12.660
But then you hear a voice inside

23:12.660 --> 23:15.950
You gotta open up your vision and see the life bestowed on you

23:15.950 --> 23:18.540
Blinded by reality

23:18.540 --> 23:20.710
Broken ideology

23:20.710 --> 23:23.250
Heart in captivity

23:23.250 --> 23:25.590
Hold on, exceeding the borders within

23:25.590 --> 23:28.090
Seize your capability

23:28.090 --> 23:30.470
Endless possibility

23:30.470 --> 23:32.800
Find your individuality

23:32.890 --> 23:35.010
Take pride; let the chase begin

23:35.010 --> 23:37.680
Don't tell me what direction you think I should take

23:37.680 --> 23:39.480
I know now to find the way

23:39.480 --> 23:42.480
Don’t tell me that this sable is for my own sake

23:42.480 --> 23:44.020
Here's what I’ve got to say

23:44.020 --> 23:47.280
Don't tell me to believe the decisions you make

23:47.280 --> 23:49.490
Facing a new day

23:49.490 --> 23:51.490
So open up your blinded eyes

23:51.490 --> 23:54.490
Stop living a lie and start living your life

23:54.490 --> 23:56.830
My way or no way

23:56.830 --> 23:59.290
Today you’re falling away

23:59.290 --> 24:01.620
My way or no way

24:01.620 --> 24:04.920
Today I’m breaking away

24:04.960 --> 24:09.960
Episode 19

24:04.960 --> 24:09.960
The Black Sunset
